WEBVTT

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:09.980
This is a work of fiction based on research into the period in which it is set. The people,
 organization, laws, and names that appear in it have no relation to any in the real world.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:28.290
Hell...

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:41.310
...might be preferable.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:47.640
A Midsummer Night's Dream Gone By

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.070
What should we do? Break through?

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:59.740
Maybe if it were just us, but not
with baggage we can't let break

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:02.910
and an extra burden slowing us down.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:05.750
I don't remember asking you to follow me.

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:08.250
Brats should watch their mouths.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:10.040
I'm not a child.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:12.800
That's just what a brat would say.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:16.550
Umm, let's all try to work together.

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:19.140
Everyone's waiting with empty stomachs.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:20.010
Oh,

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:23.100
one of the stuffy bastards sniffed us out.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.180
I'll rush out as a decoy.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:28.350
You two escape to Tenmanya in the meantime!

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:32.400
Vampires!

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.940
There are two roads open to you!

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:38.160
Will he be okay?

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:41.700
Kurusu should manage fine on his own.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.370
Stick close to me.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.250
I'm not a child.

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:56.840
It's not beautiful.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:07.100
Oh, found you!

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.480
Where have you been?

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.900
Where? Just for a walk.

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:15.030
How many times have I told you
it's dangerous at night?

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:18.150
I came back in one piece, so does it matter?

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:19.280
What is it now?

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:20.110
Well,

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:24.580
I need a favor only you can do, Defrott.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:27.080
Can I refuse?

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:28.750
Ta-dah!

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:30.210
Here!

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:32.460
That's Misaki's...

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.000
The costume miraculously survived the fire!

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.260
I want to use this for Eurydice.

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:39.260
You're doing <i>Orpheus</i>?

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:40.680
Where?

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:43.050
Here!

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:45.220
We're putting on a play!

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:52.690
Oh, I can picture it.

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:55.900
I can see you playing the lyre.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:59.700
I'm playing Orpheus?
That's the first I've heard of it.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:02.660
I decided on it! Just now!

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:04.830
Don't make that face.

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:07.120
I want to cheer everyone up!

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:11.040
Everyone feels hopeless.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:15.540
A lot of people haven't even
figured out where they're going to go.

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:16.170
So--

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:16.880
Fine.

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:17.710
Huh?

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:22.010
<i>Orpheus </i>isn't my idea of an interesting play,

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:26.760
but if I can change the ending
with Eurydice, I'll consider it.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.180
You'll do it?!

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:32.190
I want to dream, too.

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:35.810
And on stage, my dreams can come true.

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:41.990
This is easy to understand.

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:48.080
It includes each member's history,
family background, and even friendships.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:53.080
Do you really need files on
Code Zero's vampires at this point?

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:57.040
If there were a pebble in your boot,
wouldn't you want to know about it?

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:01.260
I'm glad to hear you
consider them a mere pebble.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:05.300
I have the vampire units you made, sir.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:09.890
But we're plagued with people
who don't understand their value.

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:14.810
The way their principles waver,
Japan's future is dark.

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:19.980
Don't we have you and your vampire units
to cut through that darkness?

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:23.400
Please, leave removing pebbles to me.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.910
Yes, I'm counting on you.

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:31.660
With Maeda gone, only you
can command the vampire units.

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:33.620
Thank you very much.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:37.460
I will strive to meet your expectations.

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:42.170
I can't believe this survived that fire.

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:45.550
It looks like the spare costumes
were packed in boxes.

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:47.890
This will be perfect for Eurydice!

00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:51.430
Oh, good idea. "Fine feathers make fine birds"!

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:53.140
I'm not playing her.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:55.310
I want to see Defrott perform!

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:57.650
But we'll need more costumes.

00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:00.360
Shepherds, guards of Hades...

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:01.690
There's more?!

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:04.990
Still, why do you have
to recruit through my paper?

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:07.870
What's wrong with that? It's a public service!

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:09.620
It's for the common good!

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:12.910
If you do something useful,
society will recognize you!

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:16.670
"Oh, that play the Nitto News put on that time

00:07:16.670 --> 00:07:18.960
gave me courage!

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:21.210
I'll subscribe as long as I live!"

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:23.050
It'll double your circulation!

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:24.920
Talk about over-optimistic.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:28.590
Well, I hope it works out, but times are tough.

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:30.930
I'll do what I can.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:33.850
Thank you so much, boss!

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:41.070
I wish I could have seen Misaki
play Salomé one more time.

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:50.700
Pull me up.

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:53.120
Kurusu, pull on the rope.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:54.290
Got it.

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:09.470
Are you mad, Takeuchi? Why send
a vampire to search underwater?

00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:11.390
I'm so glad the box in intact.

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:12.090
Hey!

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:13.560
Now, now.

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:16.310
Let's get this to Mr. Tenmanya quickly.

00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:18.440
I want to see inside, too.

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.820
This is the last one.

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:25.280
Okay, it's open!

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:27.030
Hey, can we open them?

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:29.240
That's what we recovered them for!

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:30.240
Wait!

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:35.580
Okay.

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:36.950
Here goes!

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:42.330
Ah! It looks like they're intact.

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:44.710
What's this?

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:47.210
A prototype skunk ball.

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:48.760
Stop! Don't throw it!

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:50.680
Why not?

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:52.090
Stop!

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:53.180
--Stop!
--Come on.

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:54.510
--Don't toy with me!
--Come on.

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:57.600
What's this?

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:59.940
Plans for a flying machine.

00:08:59.940 --> 00:09:00.980
Wow.

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:02.940
Want to try flying?

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:04.190
Can I?

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:08.110
Yes, an A class like you should be able to.

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:11.320
I think there's enough
material to build it here.

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:13.200
Want to give it a try?

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:14.740
It sounds like fun!

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:17.830
Nothing but junk, I see.

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:21.620
But the most important thing is right here.

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:27.960
The blood the vampire units were based on.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:29.210
This?

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:31.260
It hasn't gone bad?

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:33.340
That's the strange thing.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:39.600
It always maintains the same appearance,
never spoiling or coagulating.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:43.770
But of course, it does
explode if sunlight hits it.

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:46.980
My eye learned that lesson.

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:49.650
What did you recover it for?

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:52.820
To find out what vampires are.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:56.700
I think this blood is influenced by sunlight,

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:00.700
or rather, by the ultraviolet rays in sunlight.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:03.460
If ultraviolet rays cause death,

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:09.880
then depending how they're used,
it may be possible for vampires to age.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:12.510
We could get older?

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:14.970
You might die, though.

00:10:17.180 --> 00:10:19.350
I don't think I'd mind.

00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:21.770
When can you do it? Tomorrow?

00:10:21.770 --> 00:10:24.140
Nowhere near that soon.

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:27.520
But I don't think it will be
too far in the future.

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:32.530
Just another 200... No, 100 years should do it.

00:10:32.530 --> 00:10:36.410
We have unlimited time, if nothing else.

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:39.410
This far enough?

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:41.910
Thank you, Santaro.

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:44.330
We'll take it from here.

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:48.090
Still, what do you need all this bamboo for?

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:51.170
Some craftsmen I'm sheltering asked for it.

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:54.010
They say they want to make a big kite.

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:56.260
Well! That sounds fun.

00:10:56.260 --> 00:11:01.520
This bamboo would make a kite
big enough to shock Goemon Ishikawa.

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:02.720
Yes.

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:04.810
The craftsmen will be delighted.

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:06.810
Flying a kite, huh?

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:09.270
I hope business soars to match.

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:15.070
It might all be fine next year,
once the vampire panic dies down, but...

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:16.700
It should be fine.

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:18.870
I have hope for next year.

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:22.490
If you say so, I'm sure it will be.

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:24.370
Well, thanks for your business!

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:25.710
You're welcome.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:35.670
What are you doing?

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:38.140
Just looking.

00:11:38.140 --> 00:11:40.760
Do you want to be an adult?

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:42.510
A human one.

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:45.060
You'll have to dream it.

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:48.150
Can vampires dream?

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:52.570
I've never tried it myself.

00:11:52.570 --> 00:11:57.530
"Life is never fully explained, my dear.”

00:11:57.530 --> 00:11:58.910
What's that mean?

00:11:58.910 --> 00:12:01.620
Suwa, do you have a moment?

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:03.080
I know this is sudden,

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:05.750
but they want you to carry
more packages tonight.

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:07.750
Got it. I'll leave now.

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:19.420
{=2}Orpheus
Orpheus: Defrott
Eurydice: Chiyo Sanjo

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:26.100
A world without good is Hell,

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:28.940
so why should I fear Hades?

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:34.690
Magnificent. I'd expect no less.

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:36.570
Why are you here?

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:38.490
I was invited.

00:12:38.490 --> 00:12:41.570
Aoi Shirase, was it?

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:43.580
I'm her guest.

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:46.830
Could you please just leave?

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:50.210
I have no desire to ever
associate with you again.

00:12:50.210 --> 00:12:52.420
I'm just saying hello.

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:55.590
I don't plan to associate with you either.

00:12:55.590 --> 00:13:01.140
I simply can't pass a noble vampire
without paying my respects.

00:13:01.140 --> 00:13:04.300
I wish you a lovely trip to Hades.

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:10.850
Uh, Orpheus, it's about time.

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:13.440
Umm, is something the matter?

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:20.240
Lighting, check.

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:22.030
Scenery, check.

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:24.700
Now we just need actors.

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:37.960
It's awfully bright.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:42.010
They're putting on an all-night play
at the Imperial Hotel.

00:13:42.010 --> 00:13:43.590
Mr. Tenmanya mentioned it.

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:44.470
What?!

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:47.890
We can't go; we have work to do.

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:49.680
Just a peek wouldn't hurt.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:53.650
Takeuchi told me not to take my eyes off you.

00:13:53.650 --> 00:13:55.230
Come on, let's go.

00:13:56.520 --> 00:14:01.030
Well, I guess I can go anytime
once the city's back on its feet.

00:14:01.030 --> 00:14:03.820
Let's hurry and get that job over with.

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:04.820
Right.

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:11.710
Aoi, I bet you're watching that play.

00:14:21.550 --> 00:14:23.260
Eurydice!

00:14:23.260 --> 00:14:25.430
Mead of my life!

00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:28.390
Light that was with me through all my pain!

00:14:28.390 --> 00:14:30.470
Flame of my life!

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:33.140
You are my love itself!

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:37.360
My mistrust of you has ruined everything.

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:39.980
The sweet taste of honey and the light.

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:41.990
Even the flame of my life

00:14:41.990 --> 00:14:46.530
is so weak and guttering,
I could extinguish it with a breath.

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:54.160
But, o merciful god of love,

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:57.580
if you still at least feel pity
for the love we two share,

00:14:57.580 --> 00:15:00.380
lift our ashes into the night sky

00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:03.420
and make of them a single star.

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:06.640
So that other lovers will look up at it

00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:10.140
and not repeat our mistakes.

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:26.240
I really do love the stage.

00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:29.580
It allows me to taste death,
if only temporarily.

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:37.210
A thistle?

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:48.340
Rufus, what are you thinking?

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:50.640
We're back.

00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:52.770
Welcome back.

00:15:52.770 --> 00:15:55.350
How did it go?

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:56.890
See for yourself.

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:59.150
Suwa didn't go to the play, either.

00:15:59.150 --> 00:16:00.520
Shut up.

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:01.900
Any souvenirs?

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:08.110
A mask! Yay!

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:09.620
Don't cling!

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:10.530
Thanks.

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:12.030
Throw that away!

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:13.540
Good work.

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:15.830
It looks like our intel was accurate.

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:19.500
Yes. Now we can move everyone, right?

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:23.420
Yes. We just need to arrange the trains.

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:24.920
I'm doing that now.

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:26.220
Oh, that's right.

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:30.680
Mr. Takeuchi, I brought the
bamboo you asked for inside.

00:16:30.680 --> 00:16:32.430
Thank you very much.

00:16:32.430 --> 00:16:34.140
Now we can try it out.

00:16:34.140 --> 00:16:36.100
Try what out?

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:38.230
That's a surprise.

00:16:49.740 --> 00:16:53.530
It's Defrott. I have an invitation.

00:16:58.210 --> 00:17:01.920
I would look closer at him.

00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:05.210
I must look at him closer.

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:05.210
This voice...

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:10.470
I am Salomé, daughter of Herodias,
Princess of Judea.

00:17:10.470 --> 00:17:14.810
Speak again, Jokanaan.

00:17:14.810 --> 00:17:16.890
What are you playing at, Rufus?!

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:19.180
We have a matter to discuss.

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:20.890
Where is the girl?

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:22.400
Right this way.

00:17:55.600 --> 00:18:00.180
To catch a big fish, you need suitable bait.

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:03.560
You think I'm interested in humans?

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:09.110
You cling to her like
an older sister. That's enough.

00:18:09.110 --> 00:18:10.280
Silence.

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:13.160
It's you who will be silent.

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:30.380
The sun gives death equally to all.

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:37.850
I'll prepare a different death for you.

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:39.310
You needn't bother.

00:18:39.310 --> 00:18:42.310
You'll be ashes, after all.

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:46.360
Rufus,

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:50.230
have you no pride?

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:51.360
Pride?

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:55.990
I lost all that when I stopped being human.

00:18:55.990 --> 00:19:01.410
Do you know what I hate most in this world?

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:08.090
Proud vampires.

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.380
Defrott...?

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:16.140
Are you okay? You're not hurt, are you?

00:19:16.140 --> 00:19:18.390
Stay back.

00:19:18.390 --> 00:19:19.510
But you're...

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:22.930
Don't treat me like a child.

00:19:27.860 --> 00:19:29.770
Where did your pride go?!

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:33.070
I can't stand to watch this threepenny play!

00:19:33.070 --> 00:19:36.780
Turn to ash and lower the curtain.

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:38.120
Oh?

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:41.290
I see an unexpected actor has taken the stage.

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:54.880
Should I tie it here?

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:56.970
Yes, please do.

00:19:56.970 --> 00:20:00.510
Wow. It's coming along well.

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:05.430
A big kite!

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:07.230
What is this thing?

00:20:07.230 --> 00:20:08.730
A flying machine.

00:20:08.730 --> 00:20:10.980
Flying? Like, in the sky?

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:14.650
Yes! I hear that, in Europe,
airplanes are already

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:17.530
dropping bombs to turn the tide of battle.

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:22.740
I'm sure that, in this new age, he who
controls the skies will rule the world!

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:26.250
That doesn't mean vampires have to fly, too.

00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:32.210
The ground is covered in obstacles.
We can cover distance faster by air.

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:34.840
I want to fly!

00:20:34.840 --> 00:20:36.920
Do you want to try, too, Suwa?

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:39.970
You just tied cloth onto bamboo, right?

00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:44.100
It's a kite. Who'd ride one of those?

00:20:44.100 --> 00:20:49.230
I think it's more like a bat myself.

00:20:49.230 --> 00:20:50.730
Isn't it dangerous?

00:20:50.730 --> 00:20:55.820
According to my calculations,
each wing needs to be 20 meters long.

00:20:55.820 --> 00:20:58.400
But if we used iron, they'd break.

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:00.610
However,

00:21:00.610 --> 00:21:04.740
this green bamboo I stitched
together is strong and flexible.

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:07.330
It should hold up.

00:21:07.330 --> 00:21:13.630
And it should only take 30 times
the muscle of normal human to operate it.

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:15.840
A human could never use it, then.

00:21:15.840 --> 00:21:18.300
Yes, and that's where vampires come in!

00:21:18.300 --> 00:21:19.680
Right, Kurusu?

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:22.260
Huh? Me?!

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:25.430
There's no way people can fly.

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:27.140
I want to fly!

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:28.810
Yoh, too, right?

00:21:28.810 --> 00:21:30.100
Yeah.

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:32.060
I want to fly with birdies.

00:21:33.730 --> 00:21:37.190
Birds don't fly in pitch-dark skies.

00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:41.360
They fly in the sunlight, where we can't.

00:21:44.410 --> 00:21:46.790
If we go into the sunlight,

00:21:46.790 --> 00:21:50.830
we'll burn up and die.

00:21:58.300 --> 00:22:00.050
Misaki.

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:10.980
I will... eliminate vampires.

00:23:41.980 --> 00:23:46.980
Dark Wings
